course: dictionary
lesson: 14395
title: Outflow and the money it counts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Outflow is a word made of two parts: out and flow. Flow means to move steadily, like water in a river. So an outflow is something flowing out of a place. «The outflow from the lake runs into the river.» The water is leaving the lake, so outflow means water flowing out.
explain: Outflow can also be a place or pipe where something flows out. «The outflow pipe carries rainwater away from the roof.» The pipe is the outflow, because it is where the water leaves. Ask yourself: what is leaving, and where does it go?
explain: Outflow is also used for money. «The shop had a big outflow of cash this month, because it paid for new shelves.» Here outflow means money going out. Its opposite is inflow, which means money coming in. In maths, you take the outflow away from the total to find what is left.
fact: Outflow is a noun: an outflow, outflows.
fact: Outflow means water, air or another substance flowing out of a place.
fact: For money, outflow means money going out of a bank, business or country.
fact: «Outflow» can also mean the place or pipe where something flows out.
fact: The opposite of outflow for money is inflow, money coming in.
exercise: «The outflow from the lake runs into the river.» What does outflow mean here? | Fish swimming into the lake | Rain falling onto the lake | *Water flowing out of the lake | A boat sinking in the lake
exercise: A business had a big outflow of money this month. What does this mean? | Money coming into the business | Customers singing in the shop | More workers arriving at the office | *Money going out of the business
exercise: Which word is the opposite of outflow when we talk about money? | outdoor | *inflow | outfit | flowerbed
test: «The storm caused a strong outflow of air from the cave.» What does outflow mean here? | Rocks falling from the roof | *Air flowing out of the cave | Air stuck inside the cave forever | The sound of thunder
test: A tank has 50 litres of water. The outflow is 20 litres. How many litres are left? | *30 litres | 70 litres | 20 litres | 50 litres
exam: What is an outflow? | *The place or pipe where water flows out | A type of fish that lives in rivers | A loud noise made by a drain | A pipe that brings water in
